      "writtenOn": "2017-06-01T21:59:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aah, now I realized why I did not go with calling this function from button_change_deferred and used the HOOK_TICK instead.\n\nConsider the case when user enters debug mode:\n1. User holding down Vup + Vdn for \u003e10 seconds\n2. After 10 seconds, EC will start flashing the LED to indicate entry into debug mode\n3. At this point user can leave the Vup + Vdn buttons\n\nNow, if we were to rely only on button_change_deferred, then this will not be triggered until user lets go of the buttons. Another way to handle it would be to schedule a deferred call from STATE_DEBUG_CHECK to ensure that we process the buttons after DEBUG_TIMEOUT to see what their current state is. I will rework that part of the code a bit.",
      "parentUuid": "87e33a31_d9989a3d",
      "revId": "cbf6bd551f969cf5179e5a210ff436b0777640b5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
